WEBVTT

00:00.080 --> 00:01.480
Report.

00:03.960 --> 00:04.880
Report.

00:04.960 --> 00:09.320
The west gate has been breached that old thing Liu Dadao ran with his men.

00:09.760 --> 00:11.160
Bastard.

00:12.240 --> 00:14.907
You few follow me to the west.

00:24.560 --> 00:29.600
As many volunteers fled the west quickly lost its ability to resist.

00:29.880 --> 00:32.547
The Wuzhao swarmed in through the west gate.

00:33.200 --> 00:38.360
Even if you immediately send reinforcements the situation is already beyond saving.

01:09.600 --> 01:11.000
Bring torches.

01:13.000 --> 01:25.000
In the eleventh month of the 19th year of Yuankang, Yiyang fell. The Prince of Jin, Sikong Yao, set fire to the granaries and fought to the death, perishing from exhaustion on the battlefield.

01:34.000 --> 01:43.000
Shi Lang's host flooded into the city, plundering Yiyang for three days straight. Countless civilians perished, and Great Xuan's northern bastion was utterly reduced to ashes.

